# Migrations deliberately NOT applied to production yet.
#
# One migration stem per line (the filename without .sql), with the reason
# after a `#`, e.g.:
#
#   00176_drop_mcp_agent_sessions   # waits for the Phase B release to bake (task ec2bde45)
#
# `npm run check:migrations` lists held migrations as "Held (intentional)"
# instead of reporting them as drift, and fails if a held migration turns out
# to be applied already. The production apply workflow refuses to run while
# anything is listed here. Remove the line in the same change that makes the
# migration safe to apply. See docs/release-process.md → "Holding a migration
# on purpose".
